  "style": {
    "name": "Warm-wood + metal accent",
    "rationale": "A freestanding bow-and-arrow read as a tensioned arc crossed by a dead-straight diagonal shaft: spruce_planks limb forms a recurve D bulging to +x over a 30-block vertical span, a bone_block string is the inward-bowed chord between its tips, and a stripped_oak_log arrow climbs up-forward (+x/+y/+z) through the grip to sell depth in 3/4 view, capped by an iron_block head (cold metallic point) and red_concrete fletching (the single saturated spark). A dark_oak_planks grip band marks the hand; an oval stripped_oak_log plinth roots the lower limb tip so the curve-against-line silhouette stands stable from every side."
  },
